00:00:02.629 --> 00:00:04.950 align:start position:0%
in hong kong three prominent activists  have pleaded guilty as a trial begins  over their involvement in last year's  pro-democracy protests  joshua wong ivan lamb and agnes chao are  all expecting jail terms  for inciting and organizing an  unauthorized assembly  the charges are related to a protest  outside of police headquarters in june  of last year  hong kong's pro-democracy movement has  faltered since beijing imposed a  sweeping national security law on the  territory  that severely restricted political  speech  joshua wong has now been remanded in  custody but before entering  court he had a message of defiance for  supporters  neither prison boss nor election bans  nor  any other arbitrary power will stop us  from activism  what we are doing now is to explain the  value of freedom  to the world through our compassion to  whom we love  so much that we are willing to sacrifice  the freedom of our own  i'm prepare for the fin chance  of walking free may god bless hong kong  and we will continue to fight for  freedom and now it's not the time for us  khao tao to beijing  and to surrender thank you
 

